{"type":"FeatureCollection","features":[{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"South Bristol Liveable Neighbourhoods study area","note":"Traced along real OpenStreetMap road centrelines (Coronation Road, Ashton Road, Winterstoke Road, Bedminster Down Road, Bedminster Road, Saint John's Lane, Wells Road), matching Bristol City Council's published study-area map. A handful of short gaps at complex junctions (under ~500m, plus one ~1.2km gap at the Bath Bridges/Temple Meads approach roads) are bridged with straight segments where the exact connecting road wasn't identified. Where the trace ran up a side road and back, the resulting out-and-back spurs have been cut off so the ring is a simple polygon — a self-touching ring tessellates into stray triangles when filled. Not survey-accurate; no official GIS boundary is published."},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-2.595833,51.4455248],[-2.5959985,51.4455094],[-2.5960585,51.4455038],[-2.5961994,51.4454907],[-2.5962779,51.4454834],[-2.5963704,51.4454748],[-2.5968971,51.4454275],[-2.5977015,51.4453899],[-2.5980876,51.4453846],[-2.5985641,51.4454],[-2.5989314,51.4454381],[-2.5990742,51.4454638],[-2.5992444,51.4454974],[-2.5996439,51.4455782],[-2.5999432,51.4456361],[-2.6009294,51.4458053],[-2.6019549,51.4459814],[-2.602111,51.4460054],[-2.6027792,51.4461083],[-2.6035168,51.4461909],[-2.6042241,51.4462514],[-2.6051205,51.4463085],[-2.6058729,51.4462938],[-2.6059438,51.4462924],[-2.6074427,51.4461879],[-2.608446,51.4461216],[-2.6087124,51.446098],[-2.6101011,51.4459749],[-2.6115566,51.4458409],[-2.6116993,51.4458274],[-2.6125772,51.4457564],[-2.6130672,51.4457146],[-2.6136459,51.4456539],[-2.6138948,51.4456153],[-2.6141293,51.4455789],[-2.6143377,51.445526],[-2.614601,51.4454591],[-2.6148245,51.4453836],[-2.6150093,51.4453211],[-2.6153742,51.4451628],[-2.615753,51.4449585],[-2.6160644,51.4447201],[-2.6161825,51.444616],[-2.6162669,51.4445437],[-2.6163486,51.4444572],[-2.6163938,51.4444217],[-2.617246,51.4429801],[